  "supernova155": {
    "note": "0.155 engine release: native/avos is not prepared from source in the app build; the reviewed prebuilt arm64 engine (native run 41848351713, archive 42e1990b…) is installed by package-supernova156-native.py. Retired avos operations: .github/build/avos-preview414.patch, .github/build/avos-supernova135.patch, .github/build/avos-supernova141-chapters.patch, .github/build/avos-supernova145-buffer-limits.patch, .github/build/avos-supernova146-upstream.patch"
  },
  "supernova156": {
    "note": "0.156: Codex Parts A-D and B17a MediaLib/FileCore changes, applied in hand-back order (docs/codex/HANDOVER.md); verified to apply cleanly on the pinned sources 5 Nov 2026."
  },
  "supernova157": {
    "note": "0.157: Codex continuation patches (six Java registrations from docs/codex/reports/2026-11-06-0157.md, in its order), then the seek-preview retriever fix and the TV-relevant NOVA 6.6.5+ changes (matching by file name, SMB share credentials, Trakt list paging and 64-bit ids, messenger folders; Samba discovery start result, network initialisation priority). Not carried: import notification change, Dolby Vision colour-fallback metadata key (clashes with this engine's keys), dependency bumps. The two native avos 0.157 patches wait for a new reviewed engine archive. Then medialib-supernova157-ledger-test (15 Nov): the ledger test's scanner gets a real files folder so the scan lock works and the test no longer depends on timing."
  },
  "supernova158": {
    "note": "0.158: medialib-supernova158-scan-queue (X4, 19 Nov): a network scan waits for the scan lease before its IO scope and five-minute source deadline start, bounded by a one-hour queue deadline instead, so queued scans wait their turn rather than timing out on 'scan lock wait interrupted'; the lease may be taken again by the thread that holds it. Then medialib-supernova158-connection-off (FL3, 19 Nov): titles under a connection turned off on Files › Connections count as excluded until it is turned on again."
  }
}
